# RetinaGrade AI - backend environment template.
#
# Copy to `backend/.env` for local development:
#
#   copy .env.example .env        (Windows)
#   cp .env.example .env          (macOS / Linux)
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed. This file is the only
# version of it that is tracked, and it contains no real values.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXACTLY ONE VARIABLE IS REQUIRED FOR A DEPLOYED API: CORS_ORIGINS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `CORS_ORIGINS` matters because the deployed frontend and the deployed API are
# different origins (two Render services), so the browser enforces CORS on every
# `/predict` and `/gradcam` call. Without this variable the backend allows
# localhost origins only, and the deployed UI fails on every prediction with a
# network error even though the API itself is healthy.
#
# Set it in the Render dashboard for the API service (render.yaml declares it as
# `sync: false`, so Render prompts for it), not in this file:
#
#   CORS_ORIGINS=https://<the static site's public URL>
#
# Comma-separated, scheme included, no trailing slash. Unset or empty is correct
# for local development and changes nothing.
#CORS_ORIGINS=
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING ELSE IS REQUIRED.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The backend needs no credentials and no host/port variables.
#
#   * Checkpoint paths are resolved from the code location, not from the
#     environment: `inference/model_loader.py` builds
#     `<backend>/models/EfficientNetB0_CFP_final.pth` and
#     `<backend>/models/EfficientNetB0_UWF_final.pt` from `__file__`, so the
#     working directory does not matter. No MODEL_DIR / MODEL_PATH style
#     variable exists in the code, so none is defined here.
#   * The listen address comes from the start command
#     (`uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`), not from an env var.
#   * CPU is mandatory and hardcoded (`main.DEVICE = "cpu"`); there is no
#     DEVICE / CUDA variable to set.
#   * The optional Gemini explanation endpoint (POST /explain) is not part of
#     this deployment: `google-genai` is not in requirements.txt, so that
#     endpoint answers 503. `/health` reports `gemini_configured: false` in that
#     case even if a key is present, because the key alone is not enough.
#     `/health`, `/predict` and `/gradcam` are unaffected.
#     To enable it: `pip install google-genai==2.28.0` in requirements.txt plus
#     GEMINI_API_KEY below.
#
# --- Gemini (optional; only if POST /explain is enabled) ---
#GEMINI_API_KEY=
#GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# --- Preprocessing override (optional, CFP only) ---
# The CFP checkpoint stores no preprocessing config at all: no image size, no
# normalization, no colour mode. Its 224 px input size and ImageNet statistics
# are therefore a documented ASSUMPTION, not checkpoint data, and every
# /predict and /gradcam response reports them as unverified.
#
# Set this ONLY if the real CFP training resolution becomes known. It changes
# the inference input size and nothing else - it never touches the weights, the
# architecture or the prediction logic. Preprocessing still reports itself as
# unverified when it is set.
#
# UWF is deliberately NOT overridable: its 512 px size is recorded in
# EfficientNetB0_UWF_final.pt and always wins.
#
#CFP_IMAGE_SIZE=224